# Shared AI Workspace

Claude Code and Codex use the same authored workspace at
`@@AI_DIRECTORY@@`.

- Put persistent, human-authored notes in `memory/`.
- Put subagent memory in `agent-memory/`.
- Put plans in `plans/`, implementation specifications in `specs/`, and reusable
  utilities in `scripts/`.
- Reusable skills live in `skills/`.
- Custom agent definitions live in `agents/claude/` and `agents/codex/`. The
  formats differ, but the roles should remain behaviorally aligned.
- Additional private or work roots may be listed in `overlays.conf`. Their
  conventional subdirectories are merged one entry at a time. Run
  `scripts/sync-overlays` after adding or removing an overlay entry.
- Claude and Codex extension directories remain open for native, tool-local
  additions. Existing same-named native entries take precedence over overlays.
- Tool-specific hook adapters live in `hooks/claude/` and `hooks/codex/`.
- Tool-specific enforcement rules live in `rules/claude/` and `rules/codex/`.
- Do not place credentials, authentication files, session transcripts, caches,
  or tool-owned databases in this workspace.
- In agents and skills intended for the public dotfiles repository, never record
  usernames, hostnames, private network addresses, employer names, or absolute
  machine paths. Private overlay content is not part of that repository.
- Do not commit or push unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not run privileged local commands. Give the user the exact command when
  privileged access is required.
